  "title": "India's GST Reforms and ITC Expansion",
  "summary": "India's GST reforms aim to expand input tax credit (ITC) coverage for businesses across sectors, including motor vehicles and energy, while addressing tax disparities and encouraging wider coverage. The reforms include provisions for group health and life insurance, with potential tax benefits for electric vehicles.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "ITC can be claimed for eligible expenses such as raw materials, motor vehicles, and energy.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Businesses are likely to benefit from ITC expansion for group health, life insurance, and electric vehicles.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The GST reforms emphasize addressing tax disparities and encouraging broader employee coverage.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
